  <Scene>
    <WorldInfo title="How Far Can a Local Idea Reach?" info="&quot;X3D Math Lab • Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.&quot;">
      <MetadataString containerField="metadata" name="mathlab.sample" reference="mathlab.x3d/1" value="&quot;{\&quot;adapter\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.x3d/1\&quot;,\&quot;axes\&quot;:\&quot;Horizontal: x within [a−R,a+R]. Vertical: sine/polynomial value; the bracket shows a pointwise bound.\&quot;,\&quot;bounds\&quot;:{\&quot;center\&quot;:[0.0,0.01666666666666672,0.0575],\&quot;size\&quot;:[5.94,3.1333333333333337,0.7150000000000001]},\&quot;configuration_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;b6b60a52378ab5e567e6d15220c5149188aab5e90be72419883c6a7c867328d8\&quot;,\&quot;insights\&quot;:[\&quot;The violet bracket is centered on the polynomial value; Taylor's theorem puts the true value inside it. Its validity comes from a derivative bound on the entire interval, not from this plot.\&quot;,\&quot;At a=0 every even coefficient vanishes. A nominal increase in degree can therefore leave the polynomial unchanged while changing this general remainder bound.\&quot;,\&quot;Increasing degree need not improve pointwise error monotonically. For sine the stated factorial remainder does tend to zero at every fixed x; a generic smooth function need not equal its Taylor series.\&quot;],\&quot;lesson\&quot;:\&quot;taylor\&quot;,\&quot;metrics\&quot;:[{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;probe_x\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Probe x\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;x=a+R·probe fraction.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:2.0},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;polynomial\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Taylor value Tₙ(x)\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:0.6666666666666667},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;error\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Signed error Tₙ(x) − sin x\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:-0.24263076015901497},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;bound\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Guaranteed pointwise |error| ≤\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;Lagrange remainder with |sin^(n+1)(ξ)|≤1; roundoff is separate.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:0.6666666666666666},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;window_bound\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Uniform window |error| ≤\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;Valid throughout [a−R,a+R], not merely at the sampled vertices.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:1.6276041666666667}],\&quot;parameters\&quot;:{\&quot;center\&quot;:0,\&quot;degree\&quot;:3,\&quot;probe\&quot;:0.8,\&quot;radius\&quot;:2.5},\&quot;sample_schema\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.sample/1\&quot;,\&quot;sample_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;13137dd9e1fb3e32b601152f0468bef7d8d20eea0ab0435dd824b3ff4ee915ea\&quot;,\&quot;scope\&quot;:\&quot;Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.\&quot;,\&quot;title\&quot;:\&quot;How Far Can a Local Idea Reach?\&quot;,\&quot;view\&quot;:\&quot;planar\&quot;}&quot;" />
